  "conclusion_stable_across_conventions": true,
  "key_findings": [
    "EO prototype alignment is not significantly better than the paper's own MMD baseline (difference 1.5 pp, p = 0.144). MMD discards EO labels entirely, so the comparison that would demonstrate transfer of class-specific optical structure is the one that does not reach significance.",
    "That comparison was underpowered: at 5 seeds it had 37% power against an effect of the observed size, so the null result is weak evidence rather than evidence of no effect. Detecting it reliably would need 15 seeds per arm.",
    "The paper's own control comparison does hold: EO prototypes beat the synthetic equiangular frame by 4.0 pp (p = 0.007), with 96% power. Note however that the two conditions also differ in learning rate and seed set; see analysis/CONFOUNDS.md.",
    "Prototype geometry alone does not help: the synthetic frame is indistinguishable from plain SAR-only fine-tuning (p = 0.661), so the gain is not explained by class separation in the loss by itself."
  ]
}
